==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*peh₁-}}
From {{inh|en|enm|penaunce}}, from {{der|en|xno|-}}, from {{der|en|fro|peneance}}, from {{der|en|la|paenitentia||repentance, penitence}}. {{doublet|en|penitence}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈpɛn.əns/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-penance.ogg|a=US}}
* {{hyph|en|pen|ance}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# A voluntary self-imposed [[punishment]] for a [[sinful]] act or wrongdoing. It may be intended to serve as [[reparation]] for the act.
#* {{RQ:Wordsworth Coleridge Lyrical Ballads|poem=The Rime of the Ancyent Marinere|passage=Quoth he, "The man hath '''penance''' done, / And penance more will do."}}
# A [[sacrament]] in some Christian churches that involves [[penitence]] (remorse plus restitution via prayer).
# Any instrument of self-punishment.
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} [[repentance]]
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} [[pain]]; [[sorrow]]; [[suffering]]

